# review_assist Active Agent Rule

Read minimally first. Do not recursively load the docs tree unless explicitly requested.

Hot context:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/core/CURRENT_STATE.md`
- active sprint/subunit file
- directly relevant domain doc from `docs/domains/README.md`

Warm context:

- `docs/core/DECISIONS.md`
- `docs/core/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/governance/TRUTH_STABILIZATION.md`
- `docs/governance/DEFERRED_WORK.md`
- `docs/governance/SPRINT_RESOLUTION.md`
- related sprint docs

Cold context:

- `docs/archive/`
- completed sprint plans
- historical/superseded planning records

Before implementation, classify the change as `SAFE LAYER CHANGE`, `DOMAIN EXTENSION`, `DOMAIN CORRECTION`, or `DANGEROUS PATCH`.

Mandatory workflows live in:

- Truth Stabilization Pass: `docs/governance/TRUTH_STABILIZATION.md`
- Deferred Work Propagation: `docs/governance/DEFERRED_WORK.md`
- Sprint Resolution & Knowledge Migration: `docs/governance/SPRINT_RESOLUTION.md`

The system generates draft, source-backed review packages. Preserve human review, provenance, uncertainty, source gaps, and no-ranking/no-selection/no-final-determination boundaries.
